course: dictionary
lesson: 7954
title: Recall: remember, call back, or return
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Recall is a word with more than one meaning, so the sentence around it tells you which one you need. To recall something means to remember it from the past. «I can recall my first day at school.» Here recall means remember.
explain: To recall someone means to order them to come back. «The ambassador was recalled» means the ambassador was told to return home. Look for clues such as «ordered», «home» or «returned» to check.
explain: A recall can also be a noun: when a company asks people to bring back a product because it is faulty or unsafe. «A recalled toy has been found to be dangerous» is a warning to stop using it. Test your meaning by swapping it into the sentence to see if it still makes sense.
fact: Recall (verb) means to remember something from the past.
fact: Recall (verb) can mean to order someone to come back, as in «The ambassador was recalled».
fact: A recall (noun) is when a company asks people to return a product because it is faulty or unsafe.
fact: Recall (noun) can also mean the ability to remember, as in «good recall».
fact: In school, a recall question asks you to remember facts you have learned, such as times tables or spellings.
exercise: «Recognising a word when reading is easier than recalling its spelling.» What does recalling mean here? | *Remembering | Buying a new book | Reading the word aloud | Crossing out the word
exercise: «Stop using a toy that has been recalled (the maker has asked for it back).» What does recalled mean here? | The toy is brand new | The toy has been painted again | The toy has been bought by a new family | *The maker has asked for it back, because it may be unsafe
exercise: «Coming back when called, called recall, is one of the most important things a dog learns.» What is recall in this sentence? | Sitting very still | *Coming back when called | Barking loudly at strangers | Chasing a ball across the park
test: Jade says, «I can't recall the spelling of necessary.» What does recall mean? | *Remember | Shout loudly | Forget completely | Return a faulty product
test: A product recall is when? | *A company asks people to return an unsafe product | A dog comes back when called | A child remembers a birthday party | A shop gives a discount on toys
exam: «Dawn services recall the landing at Gallipoli at dawn in 1915.» What does recall mean here? | To order back | To repeat a sound | To return a product | *To remember and honour
